.TH MNEMOND 1 "2026-04-04" "mnemond" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mnemond \- persistent, searchable memory daemon for LLM agents via MCP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mnemond
.RB [ \-\-stdio " | " \-\-daemon " | " \-\-foreground ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-gpu ]
.br
.B mnemond
.B \-\-gen\-key
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.br
.B mnemond
.B \-\-rebuild\-indexes
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.br
.B mnemond
.B \-\-check\-config
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.br
.B mnemond
.RB [ \-\-version " | " \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mnemond
is a UNIX daemon that provides persistent, searchable memory to LLM agents
via the Model Context Protocol (MCP).
It combines a bi-temporal knowledge graph (LMDB), full-text search
(SQLite FTS5), and vector similarity search (usearch HNSW) into a single
process with zero cloud dependencies.
.PP
In the default
.B \-\-stdio
mode, the daemon communicates over stdin/stdout using newline-delimited
JSON-RPC, suitable for use as an MCP subprocess.
In
.B \-\-daemon
or
.B \-\-foreground
mode, it listens for HTTP connections using the Streamable HTTP MCP transport
(MCP\ 2025\-03\-26).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stdio
Run in the foreground with MCP over stdin/stdout.
This is the default mode.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Daemonize (fork, setsid).
Logging switches to syslog after the fork.
Requires
.B [http] enabled = true
in the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground without stdio.
Listens for HTTP connections.
Requires
.B [http] enabled = true
in the configuration file.
Supports
.BR systemd (1)
socket activation via
.BR sd_notify (3).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " "\-\-config \fIfile\fR"
Path to the configuration file.
Overrides the default search path (see
.BR "CONFIGURATION" ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rebuild\-indexes
Rebuild the FTS5 and usearch indexes from the authoritative LMDB store,
then exit.
Useful after a crash or when upgrading index formats.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-no\-gpu
Skip GPU/NPU hardware detection at startup.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-check\-config
Validate the configuration file and exit.
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-gen\-key
Generate a cryptographically secure MCP authentication token and write it
to the configuration file.
The 256-bit token (64 hexadecimal characters) is read from
.I /dev/urandom
and inserted as the
.B auth_token
value in the
.B [http]
section of the configuration file.
.IP
If the configuration file already contains an
.B auth_token
line, it is replaced.
If the
.B [http]
section exists but has no
.B auth_token
line, one is added.
If no
.B [http]
section exists, one is appended.
If no configuration file exists at all, a minimal one is created with
.B [http] enabled = true
and the generated token.
.IP
The token is printed to standard output (for capture by scripts),
and a confirmation message is printed to standard error.
.IP
Use
.B \-\-config
to specify which file to write to; otherwise the standard search path
is used, defaulting to
.IR ~/.config/mnemond/mnemond.conf .
Parent directories are created as needed.
.IP
Example:
.RS
.nf
.B "mnemond \-\-gen\-key"
.B "mnemond \-\-gen\-key \-\-config /etc/mnemond/mnemond.conf"
.B "TOKEN=$(mnemond \-\-gen\-key)"
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B mnemond
reads an INI-format configuration file.
The search path is:
.PP
.RS
.PD 0
.IP 1. 4
Path given by
.BR \-\-config
.IP 2.
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mnemond/mnemond.conf
.IP 3.
.I ~/.config/mnemond/mnemond.conf
.IP 4.
.I /etc/mnemond/mnemond.conf
.PD
.RE
.PP
A missing configuration file is not an error; all settings have defaults.
The tilde character
.RB ( ~ )
is expanded to
.IR $HOME .
Lines beginning with
.B #
or
.B ;
are comments.
.PP
An annotated example is installed as
.IR mnemond.conf.example .
.SS General
.TP
.B data_dir
Path to the data directory.
Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/mnemond .
.TP
.B log_level
Logging verbosity:
.BR debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
Default:
.BR info .
.TP
.B foreground
Run in foreground mode.
Default:
.BR false .
.SS LMDB
.TP
.B map_size_gb
Maximum database size in gigabytes (virtual, not pre-allocated).
Default:
.BR 10 .
Valid range: 1\-1024.
.TP
.B max_readers
Maximum concurrent LMDB readers.
Default:
.BR 64 .
.SS Embedding
.TP
.B model_path
Path to the GGUF embedding model.
Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/mnemond/models/nomic-embed-text-v1.5.Q8_0.gguf .
.TP
.B dimensions
Embedding vector dimensions.
Default:
.BR 768 .
Valid range: 1\-4096.
.TP
.B batch_size
Batch size for embedding generation during consolidation and bulk operations.
Default:
.BR 32 .
.TP
.B gpu_layers
Number of model layers to offload to GPU.
Set to 99 to offload all layers when a GPU is available.
Default:
.BR 99 .
.TP
.B model_sha256
Optional SHA-256 hash for model file integrity verification.
Default: empty (no verification).
.SS Extraction
.TP
.B enabled
Enable entity extraction via an external LLM endpoint.
Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B endpoint
URL of the chat completions endpoint.
Default:
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions .
.TP
.B timeout_ms
Request timeout in milliseconds.
Default:
.BR 10000 .
.TP
.B model
Model name to pass to the endpoint.
Default: empty (use server default).
.SS Search
.TP
.B default_top_k
Default number of results returned by search.
Default:
.BR 10 .
.TP
.B max_top_k
Maximum allowed
.B top_k
value.
Default:
.BR 50 .
Valid range: 1\-200.
.TP
.B rrf_k
Reciprocal Rank Fusion constant.
Default:
.BR 60 .
.SS Consolidation
.TP
.B threshold
Number of unconsolidated memories before auto-triggering consolidation.
Default:
.BR 100 .
.TP
.B interval_sec
Periodic consolidation interval in seconds.
Default:
.BR 3600 .
.TP
.B similarity_threshold
Cosine similarity threshold for clustering during consolidation.
Default:
.BR 0.7 .
.SS Decay
.TP
.B half_life_days
Number of days for memory importance to halve without access.
Default:
.BR 90 .
.TP
.B min_importance
Importance score below which memories are eligible for pruning.
Default:
.BR 0.01 .
.SS Import
.TP
.B allowed_paths
Colon-separated list of directories that
.B import_file
and
.B import_directory
tools may read from.
Default:
.BR ~ .
.TP
.B max_batch_size
Maximum number of memories per
.B import_batch
call.
Default:
.BR 1000 .
.TP
.B default_chunk_size
Default maximum characters per chunk during import.
Default:
.BR 4096 .
.TP
.B writer_batch_size
Memories per writer queue submission to avoid blocking.
Default:
.BR 50 .
.SS Security
.TP
.B detect_secrets
Enable FSM-based secret pattern detection in stored content.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B max_memory_size_kb
Reject memories larger than this value in kilobytes.
Default:
.BR 64 .
.SS Threads
.TP
.B reader_pool_size
Number of reader threads.
Set to 0 for automatic detection (min of CPU count and 16).
Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B write_queue_depth
Maximum depth of the writer queue.
Default:
.BR 1024 .
.SS HTTP
.TP
.B enabled
Enable the HTTP transport.
Required for
.B \-\-daemon
and
.B \-\-foreground
modes.
Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B bind
Address to bind the HTTP listener to.
Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B port
TCP port for the HTTP listener.
Default:
.BR 3847 .
.TP
.B max_connections
Maximum concurrent HTTP connections.
Default:
.BR 32 .
.TP
.B auth_token
Static Bearer token for HTTP authentication.
Required when
.B bind
is set to a non-localhost address.
Clients must include an
.B "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
header.
Can be generated with
.BR "\-\-gen\-key" .
Default: empty (no authentication).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM\fR, \fBSIGINT
Initiate graceful shutdown.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration file.
Currently reloads the log level.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Dump statistics (memory, entity, edge, and index counts) to the log.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.SH MCP TOOLS
.B mnemond
exposes 28 functional MCP tools and 4 honeypot decoy tools.
The functional tools include:
.PP
.B Memory management:
store_memory, retrieve_memory, update_memory, delete_memory, list_memories,
search_memories, batch_store
.PP
.B Knowledge graph:
add_entity, get_entity, update_entity, delete_entity, list_entities,
add_edge, get_edges, delete_edge, traverse_graph
.PP
.B Search and retrieval:
search_memories, search_entities, hybrid_search
.PP
.B Import:
import_file, import_directory, import_batch
.PP
.B Maintenance:
consolidate, rebuild_indexes, get_stats, get_memory_health
.PP
.B Temporal:
time_travel_query, temporal_diff
.PP
See the MCP tool schema (via
.BR initialize )
for full parameter documentation.
.SH TRANSPORTS
.SS stdio
Newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout.
Selected with
.B \-\-stdio
(the default).
Logging goes to stderr only.
.SS Streamable HTTP
HTTP POST/GET/DELETE on the
.I /mcp
endpoint.
Conforms to MCP\ 2025\-03\-26.
Sessions are tracked via the
.B Mcp\-Session\-Id
header.
Bearer token authentication is supported.
Origin validation prevents CSRF.
.SH STORAGE
LMDB is the source of truth.
FTS5 (full-text search) and usearch (vector similarity) are derived
indexes and can be rebuilt with
.BR \-\-rebuild\-indexes .
.PP
Serialization uses hand-rolled MessagePack with short map keys and a
version byte per record.
IDs are UUIDv7 (RFC\ 9562), providing time-sortable 16-byte binary keys.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mnemond/mnemond.conf
Default user configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/mnemond/mnemond.conf
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mnemond/
Default data directory (LMDB, SQLite, usearch indexes).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mnemond/models/
Default embedding model directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (configuration error, storage error, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run as an MCP subprocess (default):
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B mnemond
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate an auth token and start as a daemon:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "mnemond \-\-gen\-key"
.B "mnemond \-\-daemon"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a key for a specific config file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "mnemond \-\-gen\-key \-\-config /etc/mnemond/mnemond.conf"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Capture the generated token in a script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "TOKEN=$(mnemond \-\-gen\-key)"
.B "echo \(dqUse Bearer $TOKEN to authenticate\(dq"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "mnemond \-\-check\-config \-\-config /etc/mnemond/mnemond.conf"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run in the foreground with a custom config:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "mnemond \-\-foreground \-\-config ./mnemond.conf"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rebuild indexes after a crash:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "mnemond \-\-rebuild\-indexes"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send SIGUSR1 to dump stats:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "kill \-USR1 $(pidof mnemond)"
.fi
.RE
